WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
- So I got this guy's
number the other night

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:04.022
And I don't know if I should wait

00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:05.967
for him to call me or I should call him

00:00:05.967 --> 00:00:08.387
- This is totally, pretty basic stuff.

00:00:08.387 --> 00:00:10.477
There's a scientific formula for this

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.148
- Max, there's no science
to this sort of thing.

00:00:12.148 --> 00:00:13.588
You just have to feel it!

00:00:13.588 --> 00:00:14.772
Definitely not now.

00:00:14.772 --> 00:00:16.769
But soon. Don't wait too long

00:00:16.769 --> 00:00:18.348
Nope. No dude!

00:00:18.348 --> 00:00:20.089
Just look inside yourself!

00:00:20.089 --> 00:00:23.818
- The universe will give me a sign.

00:00:23.818 --> 00:00:25.046
Woah!

00:00:25.046 --> 00:00:26.680
Woah! Did you see that man?

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:27.730
- See what?

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:29.889
Right there! Right outside our window!

00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:31.793
There's a crazy looking guy

00:00:31.793 --> 00:00:35.438
- Ok so if the guy is G, and time is X

00:00:35.438 --> 00:00:37.737
then you just divide the number of hours..

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.223
- No, no, no

00:00:39.223 --> 00:00:40.848
We need to take into consideration

00:00:40.848 --> 00:00:42.914
We both have each others' numbers

00:00:42.914 --> 00:00:45.097
and that we met on a Sunday

00:00:45.097 --> 00:00:47.396
which is the start of a work week..

00:00:47.396 --> 00:00:49.305
Wait!

00:00:50.925 --> 00:00:52.945
- Woah, it's my phone!

00:00:52.945 --> 00:00:54.176
What's my phone doing out here?

00:00:54.176 --> 00:00:54.893
(startled noise)

00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:55.750
Who are you?

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:59.523
You're my spirit guide, aren't you?

00:00:59.973 --> 00:01:01.706
How do I know when to call her?

00:01:01.706 --> 00:01:03.502
- (goofy laugh)

00:01:03.502 --> 00:01:04.962
- I've got her number right here

00:01:04.962 --> 00:01:06.588
- (goofy laugh)

00:01:08.449 --> 00:01:09.125
- Where'd he go?

00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:12.004
- (inaudible yell)

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.256
- For the past five weeks

00:01:14.256 --> 00:01:15.858
The fifth obituary in the LA Times

00:01:15.858 --> 00:01:18.714
in 2015 has started

00:01:18.714 --> 00:01:22.615
with the fifth letter in the alphabet, E.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.729
Look at this crossword puzzle

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:26.446
The place five down, five across

00:01:26.446 --> 00:01:28.048
with all E's.

00:01:28.048 --> 00:01:29.441
- Hold on this is getting out of hand.

00:01:29.441 --> 00:01:32.019
- How many fingers on your hand?

00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:34.626
Five!

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.900
- Where are you?

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.757
- Hello!

00:01:39.757 --> 00:01:42.311
- How do you keep doing that?

00:01:42.311 --> 00:01:44.633
Are you saying bananas bruise quickly?

00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:46.050
That I should call while the time is ripe?

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.929
Oh! Ow!

00:01:48.929 --> 00:01:49.649
What?

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:50.810
Where did you go?

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.701
(inaudible yell)

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:55.410
- Same white van has
driven by three times now

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:56.098
They're onto us

00:01:56.098 --> 00:01:56.963
Quick turn the phones off

00:01:56.963 --> 00:01:58.123
We need to turn both of our phones off!

00:01:58.123 --> 00:01:59.888
- Then how will you know
if he is calling you?

00:01:59.888 --> 00:02:01.197
- Damnit! You're right!

00:02:01.197 --> 00:02:03.975
It's not just an equation for when to call

00:02:03.975 --> 00:02:05.461
it's connected to everything!

00:02:05.461 --> 00:02:07.249
It's bad.. It's really bad.

00:02:07.249 --> 00:02:09.510
- I need to call someone for you.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.486
I legitimately think that you might be

00:02:11.486 --> 00:02:13.021
losing your mind.

00:02:14.419 --> 00:02:16.045
- What does it mean?

00:02:16.045 --> 00:02:17.949
Why is it a banana?

00:02:17.949 --> 00:02:19.156
Why did I follow you here?

00:02:19.156 --> 00:02:21.799
When should I call?

00:02:25.469 --> 00:02:29.007
(inaudible yell)

00:02:29.007 --> 00:02:31.880
- Wait! I'll just call him.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.200
Yeah. Let's do this in
15, I'll just call him.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.383
- What the...?

00:02:37.383 --> 00:02:42.383
Oh! I'll just call her!

00:02:43.275 --> 00:02:44.645
I'll just call her.

00:02:44.645 --> 00:02:47.069
Oh she's calling me!

00:02:47.069 --> 00:02:48.628
Hello? Hey!

00:02:48.628 --> 00:02:49.301
- Hey!

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:51.554
- I was literally just about to call you

00:02:51.554 --> 00:02:54.827
and, I would like to
go to dinner with you.

00:02:54.827 --> 00:02:56.298
Yeah. What time is good for you?

00:02:56.298 --> 00:02:58.328
(rock music)

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.470
- What about five?

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.581
- Ok, yeah that seems a little early

00:03:03.581 --> 00:03:05.787
but yeah, that's fine! Five is great.

00:03:05.787 --> 00:03:09.032
Awesome! Weird day..

00:03:10.593 --> 00:03:11.818
- Banana!

